      "a": "wer:\nYes, the ideas of Upanishadic thinkers were different from those of the fatalists and materialists. Upanishadic thinkers focused on understanding the self (atman), rebirth, and consequences of actions (karma). Fatalists believed everything is predetermined, while materialists denied existence beyond the material world and did not accept rebirth or the soul\u2019s existence."
