      "a": "wer:\nThe ruins of Hampi have been studied using various methods. In 1800, Colin Mackenzie prepared the first plan of the site, depending on local memories and shrines. Later, photographers, from 1856 onwards, documented the monuments. Epigraphists compiled inscriptions, and information was also obtained from accounts of foreign travellers and literature in Telugu, Kannada, Tamil, and Sanskrit. These archaeological and documentary methods complemented the oral testimonies of priests from the Virupaksha temple, providing a fuller, multi-dimensional understanding of Vijayanagara\u2019s social, cultural, and architectural past. The combination ensured more accuracy and a broader perspective about the site\u2019s history and importance."
